# width: 120
# height: 40
# daily: the Settings overlay names the focused row's destination file
# in its title — a genuinely good idea in an app that splits settings
# between a workspace file and a home file. A workspace-scope row got
# the tidy relative form (`→ .mnml/config.zon`); a home-scope row got
# the RAW ABSOLUTE path, which the box then chopped mid-path with no
# ellipsis, so the one thing the title exists to say — which file this
# row writes — is the part that got cut
# (hunt/findings-2026-09-21/daily-settings-title-truncated.md).
#
# `$HOME` reads as `~` now, and a subtitle that still does not fit is
# cut from the LEFT so the file name survives.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
command view.settings
# A workspace-scope row: the title names the file, and it fits.
expect screen contains "Settings · → .mnml/config.zon"

# A home-scope row. `Launcher dock edge` is `ui.dock.edge`, home scope.
key /
type "dock edge"
key enter
expect screen contains "▸ Launcher dock edge:"
# The title still ends in the file it writes, whatever the path's head
# had to give up to fit.
expect screen contains "config.zon"
expect screen contains "Settings · → "
key esc
